$\begin{align}
\blueE{25\%} \text{ of }\maroonD{520} &= \blueE{\dfrac{25}{100}} \cdot \maroonD{520}\\\\
&=\blueE{\dfrac{1}{4}} \cdot \maroonD{520}
\end{align}$

$\blueE{25\%}$ of a number *always* equals $\blueE{\dfrac{1}{4}}$ of the number.

What is $\blueE{\dfrac{1}{4}}$ of $\maroonD{520}$?
